From f863821a497ef974ba09a6d96c1821f5f81e8403 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:16:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] GX core: the derived pipeline cache keyed by a register
 version, and the worker's batch buffer kept

build_draw_plan_into's cache of the pipeline state derived from the BP, VCD
and VAT registers built a 2 KB key at every draw - every BP register and its
valid flag, zeroed, copied and compared - thousands of draws a frame. The
state now carries a version that apply() changes whenever it changes one of
those registers (a write of the same value does not); a version comes from
the thread's own count tagged with the thread, so it is never reused, and a
copy of the state carries its registers' version. The cache compares that
version and the vertex format, then the draw's own transform, channel, light
and texture values, as before.

The FIFO worker took a new vector for each batch, so the handoff it swapped
back had no capacity: the game thread grew it again at every publish and the
worker freed the old one. The worker's vector now lives across batches.

With the host's graphics resolver cache (Wind Waker Recomp), the translation
worker stopped being the limit at native 60 Hz on Outset (Windows): 57.0 to
59.7-60.0 updates a second, the game thread's drain waits 48-71 ms a second
to 18-38.
